{
  "quest.0249C5F18EA63BD7.title": "Do Not Enter Yet",
  "quest.0249C5F18EA63BD7.quest_subtitle": "The Nether begins with a safe portal site in the Overworld",
  "quest.0249C5F18EA63BD7.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: understand the Nether's most important differences and choose a safe place for the portal frame.",
    "",
    "The Nether is another dimension. It has no normal daytime, many areas contain fire or Lava, and new hostile creatures await you. Build and check everything in the familiar Overworld first.",
    "",
    "Important: Water from a Bucket cannot be placed normally in the Nether; attempting it makes the Water evaporate immediately. Never use a Bed there—it explodes instead of setting a respawn point.",
    "",
    "Choose a flat place near home with solid ground. Keep away from storage Chests, fields, and animal pens so the arrival area remains clear. Leave enough space in front of and behind the future portal for safe arrival.",
    "",
    "Only during the ignition attempt should the immediate ignition area remain clear of wood, leaves, and other flammable blocks. If ordinary fire appears instead of the purple portal surface, you can extinguish it safely and check the frame. A successfully activated portal does not set its surroundings on fire.",
    "",
    "This first section builds only the frame. Do not light it or walk through yet. The complete equipment and safe return routine come before the first visit.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after choosing a suitable portal site with clear and safe access.",
  ],
  "task.135AD6029FB74CE8.title": "Chose a safe portal site with clear access",

  "quest.246BE713A0C85DF9.title": "Flint from Gravel",
  "quest.246BE713A0C85DF9.quest_subtitle": "Not every Gravel block drops Flint immediately",
  "quest.246BE713A0C85DF9.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold one Flint in your inventory.",
    "",
    "Gravel is a grey, grainy block that falls downward like Sand. Never dig directly beneath a Gravel ceiling. Clear it from the side or above and keep one open step behind you.",
    "",
    "A Shovel mines Gravel especially quickly. Breaking it usually drops Gravel again, but sometimes produces Flint instead. This is random; if Gravel drops, you can place it again and continue mining it.",
    "",
    "Pick up one Flint. The task completes automatically as soon as it is in your inventory.",
  ],
  "task.357CF824B1D96E0A.title": "Own 1 Flint",

  "quest.468D0935C2EA7F1B.title": "Craft Flint and Steel",
  "quest.468D0935C2EA7F1B.quest_subtitle": "One Iron Ingot and one Flint in any arrangement",
  "quest.468D0935C2EA7F1B.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: craft one Flint and Steel.",
    "",
    "Open your inventory with E. Place one Iron Ingot and the Flint in any two slots of the small 2 × 2 crafting grid. The recipe is shapeless; the two items do not have to lie diagonally as shown in the image.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/flint_and_steel.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Take the Flint and Steel from the result slot. Right-clicking can light a fire on a suitable block. Do not test it inside your house, against a wooden wall, in a forest, or beside your supplies—fire can spread.",
    "",
    "You can put out a single fire block with the left mouse button, even with an empty hand; no tool is required. Do not step into the flame, and extinguish only fire you can reach from safe ground.",
    "",
    "Keep the Flint and Steel, but do not use it on the portal frame yet.",
    "",
    "Reward: One Iron Ingot replaces the Iron used for the Flint and Steel.",
  ],
  "task.579E1A46D3FB802C.title": "Own 1 Flint and Steel",

  "quest.79B03C68F51DA24E.title": "Ten Obsidian for the Smallest Frame",
  "quest.79B03C68F51DA24E.quest_subtitle": "Crying Obsidian cannot form a Nether Portal",
  "quest.79B03C68F51DA24E.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold ten Obsidian in your inventory at the same time.",
    "",
    "Obtain Obsidian with the same safe Water-and-Lava method used for the Enchanting Table. Let Water flow over still Lava source blocks and mine the resulting Obsidian only with a Diamond or Netherite Pickaxe.",
    "",
    "Ten Obsidian are enough for the smallest working portal frame because its four corners may remain empty. A fully filled rectangular frame requires 14.",
    "",
    "Crying Obsidian has conspicuous bright purple areas and may occur in Ruined Portals. It looks similar, but cannot be part of an activatable Nether Portal frame.",
    "",
    "Hold all ten ordinary Obsidian in your inventory at the same time. The task does not consume them.",
    "",
    "Reward: 5 XP points for gathering the materials carefully.",
  ],
  "task.0AC14D79062EB35F.title": "Hold 10 Obsidian in your inventory at the same time",

  "quest.2CE36F9B2840D571.title": "Build the Portal Frame",
  "quest.2CE36F9B2840D571.quest_subtitle": "Four blocks wide and five blocks tall on the outside",
  "quest.2CE36F9B2840D571.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: build an unlit Nether Portal frame at the prepared site.",
    "",
    "The smallest frame stands vertically and measures four blocks wide and five blocks tall on the outside. Its opening is two blocks wide and three blocks tall.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/nether_portal_frame.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "The image shows a finished frame made from exactly ten Obsidian. Place the two bottom Obsidian blocks first, then both three-block-tall sides, and finally the two top blocks. Use safe stairs or Scaffolding to reach the top instead of simply jumping down.",
    "",
    "The four Dirt blocks in the image are only temporary building blocks at the corners; they are not part of the portal frame itself and may be removed after construction. The corners do not require Obsidian.",
    "",
    "Later, you will use Flint and Steel to light a fire on the lower inside of the frame. Keep the immediate ignition area clear of flammable blocks until activation succeeds. If only ordinary fire appears instead of the purple portal surface, extinguish it immediately with the left mouse button and check the frame. An active portal does not spread fire by itself.",
    "",
    "Do not use the Flint and Steel yet. First check that the frame is stable and has clear ground on both sides.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after building and checking the frame.",
    "",
    "Reward: Eight Torches and 5 XP points for the prepared portal site.",
  ],
  "task.3DF470AC3951E682.title": "Safely built an unlit 4 × 5 portal frame",

  "quest.14C1D6E29A5F730B.title": "Five Gold Ingots for the Journey",
  "quest.14C1D6E29A5F730B.quest_subtitle": "Gold Ore requires an Iron Pickaxe or a stronger tool",
  "quest.14C1D6E29A5F730B.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold five Gold Ingots in your inventory at the same time.",
    "",
    "Gold Ore has yellow inclusions in Stone or Deepslate. Mine it only with an Iron, Diamond, or Netherite Pickaxe. A weaker tool destroys the block without yielding the Gold.",
    "",
    "Without Silk Touch, it drops Raw Gold. Silk Touch is an enchantment that the Enchanting Table may randomly offer for a Pickaxe. You do not need it for this task; it merely makes the Ore block itself drop when mined.",
    "",
    "Put Raw Gold in the top slot of a Furnace and Fuel below; each Raw Gold becomes one Gold Ingot. Gold Ore collected with Silk Touch can also be smelted directly.",
    "",
    "Keep five Ingots together until the task completes. In the next step, you will make a Golden Helmet from them.",
    "",
    "Reward: Four Coal replace some of the Fuel and remain as a reserve for more smelting.",
  ],
  "task.25D2E7F3AB60841C.title": "Hold 5 Gold Ingots at the same time",

  "quest.47F40915CD82A63E.title": "A Golden Helmet for Piglins",
  "quest.47F40915CD82A63E.quest_subtitle": "One worn piece of Gold Armour prevents ordinary Piglins from attacking on sight",
  "quest.47F40915CD82A63E.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: craft a Golden Helmet and put it on.",
    "",
    "Fill the top row of the Crafting Table with three Gold Ingots. In the row below, place one more Ingot on the left and right while leaving the middle slot empty. The recipe may also sit one row lower in the grid.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/golden_helmet.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Take the Golden Helmet from the result slot and wait briefly for the item task to complete. Then open your inventory and equip the Helmet in the highest armour slot. A Helmet already worn returns to your inventory.",
    "",
    "Ordinary Piglins will not attack merely because you are present while you wear at least one piece of Gold Armour. This is not complete protection: attacks and certain actions can still anger them. Piglin Brutes in Bastion Remnants attack regardless of your clothing.",
    "",
    "Every piece of Gold Armour has this effect: Helmet, Chestplate, Leggings, or Boots. This journey uses a Helmet so that you can wear stronger Boots. Ordinary Golden Boots do not wear out through normal walking; only the later Soul Speed enchantment can consume durability on Soul Sand and Soul Soil.",
    "",
    "The Golden Helmet provides less protection and durability than a stronger Helmet. Wear your best available Armour in the other three slots.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark while the Golden Helmet is equipped in the armour slot.",
    "",
    "Reward: Five Gold Ingots replace the Gold used for the practice Helmet. Five XP points reward your preparation for Piglins.",
  ],
  "task.58051A26DE93B74F.title": "Own a Golden Helmet",
  "task.69162B37EFA4C850.title": "Wore a Golden Helmet in the armour slot",

  "quest.02495E6AB2D7F183.title": "Pack for the First Nether Visit",
  "quest.02495E6AB2D7F183.quest_subtitle": "Combat, retreat, and a protected arrival point need different supplies",
  "quest.02495E6AB2D7F183.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold all minimum equipment in your inventory at the same time.",
    "",
    "Bring one Iron, Diamond, or Netherite Sword, one Iron, Diamond, or Netherite Pickaxe, a Shield, the Flint and Steel, 32 Cobblestone, 16 Torches, and eight substantial cooked foods. Also wear the Golden Helmet and your best Armour in the other slots.",
    "",
    "If you do not have a suitable Sword, Iron is the least expensive accepted choice: place two Iron Ingots vertically and one Stick directly beneath them in the same column of the Crafting Table. An existing Diamond or Netherite Sword also satisfies the task.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/iron_sword.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "The Sword is for unavoidable close combat, the Shield for an orderly retreat, and the Pickaxe for obstacles. Use Cobblestone after arrival to build a small protected area around the portal; Torches mark it and your first short route.",
    "",
    "Keep the Flint and Steel as a reserve in case the portal later goes out. You do not need a Water Bucket for this trip: Water cannot be placed normally in the Nether. Leave several inventory slots empty so new items are not left behind.",
    "",
    "Arrange the Sword, Pickaxe, Cobblestone, Torches, and food in quickly reachable slots before approaching the portal. Put the Shield in your offhand. The task checks all required supplies together and consumes none of them.",
    "",
    "Reward: Four Bread supplement your reserve before the journey.",
  ],
  "task.135A6F7BC3E80294.title": "Hold 1 Iron Sword or better",
  "task.246B708CD4F913A5.title": "Hold 1 Iron Pickaxe or better",
  "task.357C819DE50A24B6.title": "Hold 1 Shield",
  "task.468D92AEF61B35C7.title": "Hold 1 Flint and Steel",
  "task.579EA3BF072C46D8.title": "Hold 32 Cobblestone",
  "task.68AFB4C0183D57E9.title": "Hold 16 Torches",
  "task.79B0C5D1294E68FA.title": "Hold 8 substantial cooked foods",

  "quest.2BD2E7F34B6081AC.title": "Activate the Portal—Stay Outside",
  "quest.2BD2E7F34B6081AC.quest_subtitle": "The purple surface confirms a correct frame",
  "quest.2BD2E7F34B6081AC.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: activate the Nether Portal without entering it.",
    "",
    "First check that the Golden Helmet is equipped and all your gear is ready. Stand in front of the frame without entering its opening. Right-click the top surface of either lower Obsidian block with Flint and Steel.",
    "",
    "A correct frame fills its inside opening with a purple portal surface. The four Dirt corner blocks may remain or be removed; they do not affect the portal.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/nether_portal_lit.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "If only ordinary fire appears, extinguish it immediately with the left mouse button. Then check: four blocks wide and five tall outside, two blocks wide and three tall inside, ten ordinary Obsidian, and no Crying Obsidian in the frame.",
    "",
    "The purple surface produces sounds and particles. Remaining inside it for a few moments starts the dimension change. Do not touch it yet; securing the other side will be explained first.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark once the purple surface is visible while you remain safely in the Overworld in front of the portal.",
    "",
    "Reward: 5 XP points for controlled activation without entering prematurely.",
  ],
  "task.3CE3F8045C7192BD.title": "Activated the portal without entering",

  "quest.5E05A1267B93C84F.title": "Secure the Overworld Side",
  "quest.5E05A1267B93C84F.quest_subtitle": "Clear ground, light, and an obvious route home prevent the first accident",
  "quest.5E05A1267B93C84F.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: secure the area around the Overworld side of the active portal.",
    "",
    "Stay outside the purple surface and carefully walk around the frame once. Light the ground in front of and behind the portal as well as the route back to your home.",
    "",
    "Fill holes directly beside the portal with solid blocks. Protect nearby drops with a small wall or railing and remove obstacles at head height. On both sides of the purple surface, keep a level arrival area at least two blocks tall.",
    "",
    "Do not completely enclose the exit or place blocks inside the purple surface. You must be able to step out from either direction without immediately falling, becoming trapped, or walking into a block.",
    "",
    "The active portal does not set its surroundings on fire. This work provides a safe arrival and keeps ordinary enemies away from a dark portal site; it does not require a particular building material.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when both sides, the ground, and the route home are clear, lit, and protected from immediate falls.",
    "",
    "Reward: Eight Torches and 5 XP points for the safe Overworld access.",
  ],
  "task.6F16B2370CA4D95E.title": "Secured and lit the Overworld side of the portal",

  "quest.1249E56A3FD70C81.title": "The Final Check Before Entering",
  "quest.1249E56A3FD70C81.quest_subtitle": "Respawn point, coordinates, health, and hotbar",
  "quest.1249E56A3FD70C81.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: check your return route and condition immediately before entering for the first time.",
    "",
    "First check your Bed at home. Sleeping in it at night sets or confirms your respawn point. Leave the Bed in the Overworld and never bring it into the Nether.",
    "",
    "Stand beside the portal and press F3 to open the coordinates display; some keyboards also require Fn. Write down X, Y, and Z for the Overworld side. Close the display afterwards.",
    "",
    "Store valuables that you do not need for this short trip. Fill your Hunger bar, wait in safety for missing hearts to recover, and leave several inventory slots empty.",
    "",
    "Final check: Golden Helmet equipped, other Armour worn, Shield in the offhand, and Sword, Pickaxe, Cobblestone, Torches, and food in quickly reachable slots. Keep the Flint and Steel in the inventory too.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark only after checking the Bed, portal coordinates, health, Hunger, equipment, and empty inventory slots.",
    "",
    "Reward: Two Bread remain in the inventory as an additional return reserve.",
  ],
  "task.235AF67B40E81D92.title": "Completed the full departure check",

  "quest.457C189D620A3FB4.title": "The First Step into the Nether",
  "quest.457C189D620A3FB4.quest_subtitle": "Arrive, stand still, and keep the portal in sight",
  "quest.457C189D620A3FB4.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: enter the Nether for the first time and remain directly beside the portal.",
    "",
    "Walk into the purple surface and remain there until the dimension change begins. After the loading screen, first release every movement key. Look around from your safe standing place before taking a step.",
    "",
    "Step carefully out of the purple surface but stay directly beside the portal. Sneak near an edge. Do not enter a dark passage, walk across unknown ground, or attack any creature.",
    "",
    "If Lava, a drop, or an enemy presents an immediate threat, do not try to fight or build. Return to the same portal surface and wait there for transport back to the Overworld.",
    "",
    "Minecraft detects the first dimension change automatically. If you entered the Nether earlier in this world, that part of the task may already be complete. Set the additional checkmark only when you are now standing safely beside the portal and can still see it.",
    "",
    "The next lesson secures and marks this exact arrival point before any exploration begins.",
    "",
    "Reward: 16 Cobblestone help protect the Nether side. Five XP points reward the controlled first entry.",
  ],
  "task.568D29AE731B40C5.title": "Entered the Nether",
  "task.679E3ABF042C51D6.title": "Stopped safely beside the visible portal",

  "quest.12C16D273E94F5A0.title": "Look Before You Build",
  "quest.12C16D273E94F5A0.quest_subtitle": "Lava, drops, and enemies determine the safe building area",
  "quest.12C16D273E94F5A0.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: inspect the immediate surroundings without moving away from the portal.",
    "",
    "Remain directly beside the purple surface and release the movement keys. Turn only your view and inspect the block beneath your feet first, then the floor, walls, and ceiling around the portal.",
    "",
    "Look for Lava and fire, open drops, falling Gravel, tight spaces, and nearby enemies. If you hear or see a Ghast or the standing place is immediately dangerous, return through the portal to the Overworld. Retreat is the correct solution here.",
    "",
    "The Golden Helmet only prevents ordinary Piglins from attacking merely because you are present. Do not attack anything, open unfamiliar containers, or mine Gold. Piglin Brutes remain hostile at all times.",
    "",
    "If the area is calm enough, place several Cobblestone blocks as temporary cover between the portal and open dangerous directions. Place four Torches so the portal area is easy to recognise. Do not block the purple surface.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after surveying the entire area and either returning safely or placing the first cover beside the portal.",
    "",
    "Reward: Eight Cobblestone and four Torches supplement the material for the shelter.",
  ],
  "task.23D27E384FA506B1.title": "Inspected the portal area and placed initial cover",

  "quest.5605A16B72D839E4.title": "A Shelter Around the Portal",
  "quest.5605A16B72D839E4.quest_subtitle": "Floor, walls, and a roof protect the only safe return route",
  "quest.5605A16B72D839E4.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: enclose the Nether side of the portal in a small, lit Cobblestone room.",
    "",
    "Begin with the floor. Close holes around the frame and widen narrow standing areas without working over an open edge. Sneak while placing blocks near a drop.",
    "",
    "Then build Cobblestone walls and a closed roof around the portal. Cobblestone is easy to obtain and suitable protection against ordinary Ghast fireballs. A roof also prevents a Ghast from striking the portal directly from above.",
    "",
    "Leave at least one clear standing space two blocks tall on both sides of the purple surface. The room's exit should lead to safe ground and may use a short corner or side wall as protection from direct shots.",
    "",
    "Light the interior. Torches make it readable but do not replace closed walls. Do not place blocks inside the portal surface, and use neither Water nor a Bed in the Nether.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when the floor, walls, roof, lighting, and a protected usable exit are complete.",
    "",
    "Reward: 32 Cobblestone replace some of the building material. Five XP points reward the secured return route.",
  ],
  "task.6716B27C83E94AF5.title": "Built a lit Cobblestone shelter with an exit",

  "quest.1249E5AFB61C7D28.title": "Mark the Portal and Return Route",
  "quest.1249E5AFB61C7D28.quest_subtitle": "Nether coordinates and a return test prevent disorientation",
  "quest.1249E5AFB61C7D28.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: record the Nether coordinates, mark the exit, and return to the Overworld once.",
    "",
    "Stand inside the shelter beside the portal and press F3; some keyboards also require Fn. Write down X, Y, and Z with the label ‘Nether portal’. Close the display afterwards.",
    "",
    "A normal Compass does not point reliably home in the Nether without a Lodestone. Rely on the recorded coordinates and visible markers. One horizontal block travelled in the Nether corresponds to roughly eight blocks in the Overworld, but this first return requires no calculation.",
    "",
    "Mark the inside of the exit with a simple, unmistakable pattern of Torches or Cobblestone. The marker should be visible from the room without narrowing the doorway or portal surface.",
    "",
    "A helpful route marker for the next exploration consists of two Cobblestone blocks stacked vertically. Stand on the side you arrived from while building it and attach a Torch to that side of the upper block. Later, the rule is always the same: the Torch side points back toward the portal. Repeat these markers only in safe, clearly visible places.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/nether_route_marker.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Then enter the purple surface and wait for transport. In the Overworld, confirm that you arrived at the original portal and recognise the route home. Do not re-enter the Nether for this task yet.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after returning successfully to the original Overworld portal.",
    "",
    "Reward: Four Bread and 5 XP points for the first fully checked outward and return journey.",
  ],
  "task.235AF6B0C72D8E39.title": "Marked the Nether portal and returned to the Overworld",

  "quest.236B08D1E94FA05C.title": "Back into the Shelter",
  "quest.236B08D1E94FA05C.quest_subtitle": "The first exploration begins with another complete check",
  "quest.236B08D1E94FA05C.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: return to the Nether prepared and initially remain inside the secured portal shelter.",
    "",
    "Store every valuable that this trip does not require in the Overworld again. Fill your Hunger and health and check the recorded Nether portal coordinates.",
    "",
    "Wear the Golden Helmet and the rest of your Armour. Simply wearing the Helmet and walking does not damage it, but taking damage can wear it down until it breaks. Do not rely on a nearly broken Golden Helmet as your only protection.",
    "",
    "Arrange the Shield, Sword, Pickaxe, Cobblestone, Torches, and food in quickly reachable places. Bring at least six Cobblestone and three Torches for route markers.",
    "",
    "Enter the portal, release every movement key after loading, and remain inside the lit shelter. Open the exit only when you neither see nor hear an enemy or fireball directly outside it.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you are fully equipped and standing safely inside the closed portal shelter.",
  ],
  "task.347C19E2FA50B16D.title": "Returned fully equipped to the portal shelter",

  "quest.458D2AF30B61C27E.title": "Not Every Piglin Is the Same",
  "quest.458D2AF30B61C27E.quest_subtitle": "Gold calms only one of the three important variants",
  "quest.458D2AF30B61C27E.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: distinguish ordinary Piglins, Piglin Brutes, and Zombified Piglins before leaving the shelter.",
    "",
    "Ordinary Piglins often carry gold weapons or Crossbows. Wearing at least one piece of Gold Armour prevents them from attacking merely because you are present. The Golden Helmet does not make you invulnerable.",
    "",
    "Ordinary Piglins still become angry if you attack them or an ally. Opening or breaking guarded containers and mining Gold Ore, Gold Blocks, or Gilded Blackstone can provoke them too. Do not open a Chest, Barrel, or any other unfamiliar container.",
    "",
    "Piglin Brutes have darker clothing and carry Golden Axes. They live mainly in Bastion Remnants and always attack; Gold Armour does not help against them. Do not enter a Bastion on this first route.",
    "",
    "Zombified Piglins have partly green decayed flesh and visible bone. They are usually peaceful until one is attacked, after which many nearby can respond together. Leave them completely alone too.",
    "",
    "From left to right, the image shows an adult ordinary Piglin, a Piglin Brute, a Baby Piglin, and a Zombified Piglin. Only the first is a suitable later bartering partner; the three unsuitable variants have a translucent red cross.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/piglin_comparison.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Never use an attack to identify a variant. If you are unsure, keep your distance and return to the shelter.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you can explain all three reactions. You do not need to encounter a Piglin.",
    "",
    "Reward: Four Torches supplement the material for the short marked route.",
  ],
  "task.569E3B041C72D38F.title": "I know the three important Piglin reactions",

  "quest.670F4C152D83E490.title": "Cover from Ghasts, Fire, and Lava",
  "quest.670F4C152D83E490.quest_subtitle": "Observe, step back, and place solid blocks between danger and yourself",
  "quest.670F4C152D83E490.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: know the safe response to the greatest hazards outside the portal shelter.",
    "",
    "A Ghast is a large white flying creature. Its cry often reveals it before your eyes do. When attacking, it launches a burning fireball that explodes and may leave fire behind.",
    "",
    "Do not try to knock the fireball back on this first route. Immediately move behind a closed Cobblestone wall or back beneath the roof. Ordinary Ghast fireballs break soft Nether ground more easily than Cobblestone, which is why the shelter uses it.",
    "",
    "If only one block burns on safely reachable ground, you can extinguish it without a tool by pressing the left mouse button. Never cross a ledge or approach a Lava field to do so. If you are burning or lack safe cover, abandon the route.",
    "",
    "Lava flows faster and farther in the Nether than in the Overworld. Do not dig carelessly through walls or floors beside Lava, and do not bridge across an open Lava field on this first route. Water cannot be placed on the ground here as a quick rescue.",
    "",
    "Open the protected exit only briefly and inspect the sky, ground, and both sides from cover. If one direction is unsafe, do not choose another unknown escape route; remain in the shelter and turn back.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after this safety inspection. You do not need to search for either a Ghast or Lava.",
    "",
    "Reward: Eight Cobblestone provide additional cover or replacement material.",
  ],
  "task.08105D263E94F5A1.title": "Understood the Ghast, fire, and Lava response",

  "quest.19216E374FA506B2.title": "Your First Marked Route",
  "quest.19216E374FA506B2.quest_subtitle": "Three short stages are enough for the first exploration test",
  "quest.19216E374FA506B2.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: travel no farther than three safe route markers and then return to the portal shelter.",
    "",
    "First hold at least six Cobblestone and three Torches in your inventory at the same time. The automatic tasks confirm that material for three markers was available.",
    "",
    "Leave the shelter only when the exit is clear. Keep the first marker within sight of the exit. At a safe, clearly visible place, stack two Cobblestone vertically and attach the Torch to the side of the upper block that points back toward the portal.",
    "",
    "Continue only far enough that you can still recognise the previous marker safely. Place the second and third markers before turns or junctions. Never stand beside an open drop while building.",
    "",
    "On this practice route, do not mine Gold, open containers, enter a structure, cross a Lava field, or pursue an enemy. If the safe path ends before the third marker, turn back earlier; safety matters more than the number.",
    "",
    "Turn around no later than the third marker. Follow the Torch side from post to post toward home and check the recorded portal coordinates if uncertain.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark only when you are standing inside the lit portal shelter again. An earlier safe retreat also counts.",
    "",
    "Reward: Two Bread remain as a reserve for the final return to the Overworld.",
  ],
  "task.2A327F4850B617C3.title": "Hold 6 Cobblestone for three route markers",
  "task.3B43805961C728D4.title": "Hold 3 Torches for three route markers",
  "task.4C54916A72D839E5.title": "Travelled a marked route safely and returned to the shelter",

  "quest.5D65A27B83E94AF6.title": "Return in Time",
  "quest.5D65A27B83E94AF6.quest_subtitle": "An exploration succeeds only after a safe return home",
  "quest.5D65A27B83E94AF6.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: return through the original portal to the Overworld and finish the first Nether route.",
    "",
    "Briefly check your health and return route inside the shelter. Leave the markers standing outside; they mark the same safe route for the next visit. Repair or extend them only later and never under immediate danger.",
    "",
    "Enter the purple surface and wait calmly for the dimension change. In the Overworld, confirm that you arrived at the original portal and recognise the lit route home.",
    "",
    "Store new finds, replenish food, and replace damaged equipment before another trip. An early retreat because of danger is not failure; it is the correct decision.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you are safely back at the original Overworld portal and the marked Nether route remains intact.",
    "",
    "Reward: 10 XP points for the first prepared, marked, and fully completed Nether exploration.",
  ],
  "task.6E76B38C94FA5B07.title": "Returned safely through the original portal",

  "quest.6F87C49DA50B6C18.title": "Optional: One Gold Ingot to Barter",
  "quest.6F87C49DA50B6C18.quest_subtitle": "Piglins trade without a menu or a selectable result",
  "quest.6F87C49DA50B6C18.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold one Gold Ingot ready for your first voluntary Piglin barter.",
    "",
    "This small branch is optional. It unlocks no required main path and does not ask you to enter a dangerous place. If your marked route has no safe partner, you can continue it later.",
    "",
    "One adult ordinary Piglin takes exactly one Gold Ingot, examines it for a few moments, and then throws back one random item or stack. There is no trading screen, and you cannot select the result.",
    "",
    "Gold Nuggets and other gold items do not replace the Gold Ingot for bartering. The five Ingots from the Golden Helmet reward were intended for attempts like this too; still bring only one Ingot on the first attempt.",
    "",
    "Baby Piglins can pick up gold but do not provide the normal barter. Piglin Brutes and Zombified Piglins do not barter at all. Look only for an adult ordinary Piglin.",
    "",
    "The automatic task completes as soon as at least one Gold Ingot is in your inventory.",
  ],
  "task.0098D5AEB61C7D29.title": "Hold 1 Gold Ingot for the first Piglin barter",

  "quest.11A9E6BFC72D8E3A.title": "Choose a Safe Bartering Place",
  "quest.11A9E6BFC72D8E3A.quest_subtitle": "A clear retreat, solid cover, and no Bastion visit",
  "quest.11A9E6BFC72D8E3A.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: find a safe place beside an adult ordinary Piglin along the known marked route.",
    "",
    "Repeat the previous equipment check before the portal and wear the Golden Helmet. Follow only your existing route markers; do not extend the route into unknown ground for this attempt.",
    "",
    "The bartering place needs firm level ground, a clear retreat to the portal shelter, and nearby Cobblestone cover. Keep away from Lava, fire, drops, Bastions, and every guarded container or Gold Block.",
    "",
    "Check from a distance that the Piglin is an adult ordinary one. A Piglin Brute with a Golden Axe, a small Baby Piglin, or a Zombified Piglin is not a trading partner. Abandon the attempt if such a hazard is nearby.",
    "",
    "From left to right, the image shows an adult ordinary Piglin, a Piglin Brute, a Baby Piglin, and a Zombified Piglin. Only the first is a suitable bartering partner; the three unsuitable variants have a translucent red cross.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/piglin_comparison.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "If needed, build a short Cobblestone corner that you can step behind. Do not block your route home or trap the Piglin inside the portal shelter. Luring or pushing it into the Overworld does not make a safe trader.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark only after checking the Golden Helmet, adult ordinary Piglin, firm ground, cover, and retreat. If no safe place exists, leave this optional task for later.",
  ],
  "task.22BAF7C0D83E9F4B.title": "Found a safe place beside an adult ordinary Piglin",

  "quest.33CB08D1E94FA05C.title": "Your First Piglin Barter",
  "quest.33CB08D1E94FA05C.quest_subtitle": "One Gold Ingot in, one random stack out",
  "quest.33CB08D1E94FA05C.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: give exactly one Gold Ingot to an adult ordinary Piglin, collect the return safely, and go home.",
    "",
    "Hold exactly one Gold Ingot in your main hand. From a safe distance, point the crosshair at the checked Piglin and press the right mouse button once. Take particular care not to attack with the left mouse button.",
    "",
    "The Piglin examines the Ingot for a few moments. Do not attack it, touch a guarded block, or give it a second Ingot during this time. It then throws one random item or stack onto the ground.",
    "",
    "Possible results include Blackstone, Gravel, Obsidian, Quartz, Iron Nuggets, Ender Pearls, or sometimes a Fire Resistance Potion. Nothing is guaranteed. A received Water Bottle still cannot be poured onto the Nether ground as a Water source.",
    "",
    "Collect the return only if it lands on safe ground. Do not chase an item toward a drop, fire, or Lava. Then follow the Torch sides back to the portal shelter and return through the original portal to the Overworld.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after one completed barter and a safe return. Because the result is random, you confirm this step yourself.",
    "",
    "Reward: One Gold Ingot replaces the first payment. Five XP points reward the calm and safe barter.",
  ],
  "task.44DC19E2FA50B16D.title": "Bartered once and returned safely to the Overworld",
}
